SUMMARY:Arts Village
DESCRIPTION:Friday October 2nd from 6PM – 10PM\nSaturday October 3rd from 6PM – 10PM\nKirkwood on the Square (Between College Ave and Walnut)\nThe Arts Village is where creativity comes to life during the festival weekend. Wander through a vibrant evening atmosphere filled with live art demonstrations\, interactive activities\, local and regional artists\, and a Night Bazaar celebrating handmade work\, creativity\, and community. Discover new artists\, try your hand at creative experiences\, and enjoy the energy of the festival after dark. \nDuring the festival-wide break at 8:30 PM Friday evening\, enjoy a special Taste of the IU Drumline bringing rhythm and excitement to the heart of downtown. Then on Saturday evening\, the 2026 Parade returns\, lighting up the streets with music\, movement\, and celebration once again. \nThe Arts Village is alive from 6 PM – 10 PM on Friday\, October 2nd and Saturday\, October 3rd\, 2026. This is a free event to attend. Donations are appreciated and help support the mission of the Lotus Education and Arts Foundation. \nInterested in participating as an artist? Email KP at associatedirector@lotusfest.org.
URL:https://www.lotusfest.org/event/arts-village-2026/
CATEGORIES:Arts Activity,Exhibits & Installations,Free Event
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/webp:https://www.lotusfest.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/art-village.webp
END:VEVENT
